  "pp_last_updated": "Last Updated: June 2026",
  "pp_section1_title": "1. Introduction",
  "pp_section1_content": "Welcome to PayOn. We are committed to protecting your personal information and your right to privacy. If you have any questions or concerns about our policy, or our practices with regards to your personal information, please contact us at privacy@payon.com.",
  "pp_section2_title": "2. Information We Collect",
  "pp_section2_content": "We collect personal information that you voluntarily provide to us when registering at the App, expressing an interest in obtaining information about us or our products and services. This includes identifiers (Name, DOB, SSN), financial information (Bank details, transaction history), and device data.",
  "pp_section3_title": "3. KYC & AML Compliance",
  "pp_section3_content": "As a financial service provider, we are legally required to verify the identity of our users to prevent money laundering and terrorist financing. This involves collecting government-issued IDs and performing background checks.",
  "pp_section4_title": "4. Purpose of Processing",
  "pp_section4_content": "We process your information for purposes based on legitimate business interests, the fulfillment of our contract with you, compliance with our legal obligations, and/or your consent.",
  "pp_section5_title": "5. Data Sharing",
  "pp_section5_content": "We only share information with your consent, to comply with laws, to provide you with services, to protect your rights, or to fulfill business obligations. This includes sharing with banking partners and payment processors like Stripe.",
  "pp_section6_title": "6. Data Retention",
  "pp_section6_content": "We will only keep your personal information for as long as it is necessary for the purposes set out in this privacy policy, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law (such as tax, accounting or other legal requirements).",
  "pp_section7_title": "7. Security Measures",
  "pp_section7_content": "We use appropriate technical and organizational security measures including AES-256 encryption and multi-factor authentication to protect the security of any personal information we process.",
  "pp_section8_title": "8. User Rights (GDPR/CCPA)",
  "pp_section8_content": "Depending on your location, you may have rights such as the right to access, rectify, or delete your personal data, as well as the right to data portability and to object to certain processing.",
  "pp_section9_title": "9. International Transfers",
  "pp_section9_content": "Our servers are located in various regions globally. If you are accessing our App from outside these regions, please be aware that your information may be transferred to, stored, and processed by us in our facilities.",
  "pp_section10_title": "10. Cookies and Tracking",
  "pp_section10_content": "We use cookies and similar tracking technologies to access or store information. Specific information about how we use such technologies and how you can refuse certain cookies is set out in our Cookie Notice.",
  "pp_section11_title": "11. Third-Party Websites",
  "pp_section11_content": "The App may contain advertisements from third parties that are not affiliated with us and which may link to other websites, online services or mobile applications. We cannot guarantee the safety and privacy of data you provide to any third parties.",
  "pp_section12_title": "12. Privacy Rights for Minors",
  "pp_section12_content": "We do not knowingly solicit data from or market to children under 18 years of age. By using the App, you represent that you are at least 18 or that you are the parent or guardian of such a minor and consent to such minor dependent’s use of the App.",
  "pp_section13_title": "13. California Privacy Rights",
  "pp_section13_content": "California Civil Code Section 1798.83, also known as the 'Shine The Light' law, permits our users who are California residents to request and obtain from us, once a year and free of charge, information about categories of personal information we disclosed to third parties for direct marketing purposes.",
  "pp_section14_title": "14. Policy Updates",
  "pp_section14_content": "We may update this privacy policy from time to time. The updated version will be indicated by an updated 'Revised' date and the updated version will be effective as soon as it is accessible.",
  "pp_section15_title": "15. Contact Us about this Policy",
  "pp_section15_content": "If you have questions or comments about this policy, you may email us at privacy@payon.com or by post to: PayOn Inc., 123 Finance Plaza, Suite 400, New York, NY 10001.",
  "faq_cat_general": "General Questions",
  "faq_cat_security": "Security & Privacy",
  "faq_cat_transactions": "Transactions & Limits",
  "faq_q1_title": "What is PayOn?",
  "faq_q1_answer": "PayOn is a next-generation mobile wallet designed for instant and secure financial transactions globally.",
  "faq_q2_title": "Is my money safe?",
  "faq_q2_answer": "Yes, your funds are held in regulated partner banks and protected by state-of-the-art encryption and security protocols.",
  "faq_q3_title": "How do I verify my account?",
  "faq_q3_answer": "You can verify your account by uploading a clear photo of your National ID or Passport in the 'Tier Verification' section of your profile.",
  "faq_q4_title": "What are the transfer limits?",
  "faq_q4_answer": "Limits vary by verification tier. Tier 1 users have daily limits of $500, while Tier 3 users can enjoy unlimited transactions.",
  "faq_q5_title": "Can I cancel a transaction?",
  "faq_q5_answer": "Once a transaction is confirmed and processed, it cannot be reversed. Please double-check the recipient's details before confirming.",
  "faq_q6_title": "Does PayOn work internationally?",
  "faq_q6_answer": "Yes, PayOn supports cross-border payments in multiple currencies with real-time exchange rates.",
  "faq_q7_title": "What if I lose my phone?",
  "faq_q7_answer": "Your account is tied to your identity, not just the device. You can log in from another device and instantly disable the old session for security.",
  "faq_q8_title": "Are there any hidden fees?",
  "faq_q8_answer": "No, we believe in full transparency. All fees are clearly displayed on the confirmation screen before you authorize any payment.",
  "faq_q9_title": "How do I contact support?",
  "faq_q9_answer": "Our support team is available 24/7 via the 'Contact Us' page or through live chat within the app.",
  "faq_q10_title": "Is PayOn regulated?",
  "faq_q10_answer": "Yes, PayOn operates under strict financial regulations and holds the necessary licenses in all jurisdictions where it provides services.",
  "faq_q11_title": "How do I change my account password?",
  "faq_q11_answer": "Go to 'Settings' > 'Security' > 'Change Password'. You will need to enter your current password followed by your new password twice.",
  "faq_q12_title": "What should I do if my payment failed?",
  "faq_q12_answer": "If a payment fails, first check your internet connection and balance. If the issue persists, check the 'History' tab for a specific error code or contact support.",
  "faq_q13_title": "Can I have multiple wallets?",
  "faq_q13_answer": "Currently, PayOn supports one primary wallet per verified identity to comply with financial regulations and ensure maximum security.",
  "faq_q14_title": "How do I update my personal information?",
  "faq_q14_answer": "Basic info can be updated in 'Edit Profile'. For sensitive data like your name or ID, you must contact our compliance team for verification.",
  "faq_q15_title": "How do I close my PayOn account?",
  "faq_q15_answer": "To close your account, please ensure your balance is zero and contact support. Note that financial data must be retained for 7 years by law.",
